{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","content":"Exit code 1\n# Ship as one Hermes user plugin directory, installed by npm\n\n**Status:** Accepted (2026-11-20)\n\n## Context\n\nThe routing backend, the controller and the skill are Python and Markdown\nthat run inside, or alongside, the Hermes harness. Before this decision they\nwere installed by hand into three places: the routing backend into the\nHermes source tree (wiped on every Hermes update), the controller into\n`~/.hermes/scripts/`, and the skill into a category folder under\n`~/.hermes/skills/`. The three copies drifted, and each side found the\nothers by searching a hardcoded list of paths.\n\n## Decision\n\nThe package is published to npm. Its installer copies one directory into\nthe Hermes user plugin directory (`$HERMES_HOME/plugins/tiiny-router/`).\nThat directory holds the routing backend, the controller and the skill. The\nrouting backend registers the skill itself through Hermes's plugin skill\nAPI, so nothing is written under `~/.hermes/skills/`. Every lookup between\nthe three is relative to that one directory.\n\n## Alternatives considered\n\n- **pip package.** Fits the runtime language, but Hermes runs in its own\n  Python environment and the controller runs on the system `python3`;\n  installing into the right interpreter is its own problem. npm gives a\n  zero-dependency `npx` installer that runs anywhere Node does.\n- **`hermes plugins install <git url>`.** Native, but it takes only git\n  URLs, gives us no hook to run `hermes config set`, and offers no\n  `doctor`.\n- **Separate skill copy under `~/.hermes/skills/`.** Editable by agents in\n  place, but that is exactly how the copies drifted before.\n\n## Consequences\n\n- npm delivers Python. Node is an install-time dependency only.\n- The installed copy is a snapshot: upgrading the package means running\n  `install` again.\n- The skill is read-only and namespaced (`tiiny-router:tiiny-model-routing`)\n  and disappears when the routing backend is disabled.\n- `uninstall` removes one directory.\nredeye","is_error":true,"tool_use_id":"toolu_01RShaNib1Mn3YSiphxsNKR3"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"68f65b3d-37bb-43c3-9af4-1be0edc7b1a4","uuid":"d21d47bc-51db-44ec-84ae-c25fe4337fbd","timestamp":"2026-11-21T05:43:44.251Z","tool_use_result":"Error: Exit code 1\n# Ship as one Hermes user plugin directory, installed by npm\n\n**Status:** Accepted (2026-11-20)\n\n## Context\n\nThe routing backend, the controller and the skill are Python and Markdown\nthat run inside, or alongside, the Hermes harness. Before this decision they\nwere installed by hand into three places: the routing backend into the\nHermes source tree (wiped on every Hermes update), the controller into\n`~/.hermes/scripts/`, and the skill into a category folder under\n`~/.hermes/skills/`. The three copies drifted, and each side found the\nothers by searching a hardcoded list of paths.\n\n## Decision\n\nThe package is published to npm. Its installer copies one directory into\nthe Hermes user plugin directory (`$HERMES_HOME/plugins/tiiny-router/`).\nThat directory holds the routing backend, the controller and the skill. The\nrouting backend registers the skill itself through Hermes's plugin skill\nAPI, so nothing is written under `~/.hermes/skills/`. Every lookup between\nthe three is relative to that one directory.\n\n## Alternatives considered\n\n- **pip package.** Fits the runtime language, but Hermes runs in its own\n  Python environment and the controller runs on the system `python3`;\n  installing into the right interpreter is its own problem. npm gives a\n  zero-dependency `npx` installer that runs anywhere Node does.\n- **`hermes plugins install <git url>`.** Native, but it takes only git\n  URLs, gives us no hook to run `hermes config set`, and offers no\n  `doctor`.\n- **Separate skill copy under `~/.hermes/skills/`.** Editable by agents in\n  place, but that is exactly how the copies drifted before.\n\n## Consequences\n\n- npm delivers Python. Node is an install-time dependency only.\n- The installed copy is a snapshot: upgrading the package means running\n  `install` again.\n- The skill is read-only and namespaced (`tiiny-router:tiiny-model-routing`)\n  and disappears when the routing backend is disabled.\n- `uninstall` removes one directory.\nredeye","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01RShaNib1Mn3YSiphxsNKR3","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01B5t8bBjtRDGskNmfepbRnC","type":"tool_result","content":"{\n  \"scripts\": {\n    \"test\": \"python3 -B test/test_installed_tree.py\"\n  },\n  \"devDependencies\": {\n    \"@substrate-system/redeye\": \"^0.1.8\"\n  }\n}\n./\n../\n.agents/\n.claude/\n.git\n.gitattributes\n.gitignore\n.redeye/\n.scratch/\nAGENTS.md\nCONTEXT.md\ndocs/\nLICENSE\nnode_modules/\npackage-lock.json\npackage.json\ntest/\ntiiny-router/\ntest:\ntest_installed_tree.py\n\ntiiny-router:\n__init__.py\nplugin.yaml\nreferences/\nscripts/\nSKILL.md\ntemplates/\nthinking.py\ntiers.py\n# Hermes Tiiny Router\n\nAn npm-distributed add-on for the Hermes agent harness that runs delegated\nsub-agents on a Tiiny appliance, routing each subtask to the model that fits\nits shape.\n\n## Language\n\n### Distribution\n\n**Package**:\nThe npm artifact that carries the routing backend, the controller and the\nskill, plus the installer that places them into a Hermes home.\n_Avoid_: plugin (for this meaning), module, bundle\n\n**Routing backend**:\nThe Hermes delegation provider that picks a model for each delegated task.\n_Avoid_: plugin, router plugin, delegation plugin\n\n**Controller**:\nThe command-line tool that plans a batch, locks the device, loads and\nevicts models, and releases the device.\n_Avoid_: lifecycle script, swap script, ctl\n\n**Skill**:\nThe instructions that tell a manager agent how to drive the controller and\ndelegate through the routing backend.\n_Avoid_: playbook, guide\n0001-npm-installs-a-single-hermes-user-plugin.md\n# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n# Stray upload / temp artifacts\n# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n# Auto-generated temp uploads that landed at the repo root by mistake.\nuser_file_upload_tmp_*\n*_upload_tmp_*\nuser_upload_*\n\n# Image/screenshot drops that are not part of the published artifact set.\n*.tmp.jpg\n*.tmp.png\n*_tmp