{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011ChFYY9hj4qAvrBsoAdnh9","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I've built the first version of `npx hermes-tiiny-router install`, and all five checklist items are done. `npm test` passes: 6 Node tests plus the existing Python suite. Everything is committed except `.redeye/notes.md`, as instructed.\n\n**What `install` does:**\n1. Copies `tiiny-router/` into `$HERMES_HOME/plugins/tiiny-router/` (default `~/.hermes`), skipping `__pycache__`.\n2. Writes a manifest, `.hermes-tiiny-router-manifest.json`, into that directory. It records the package name, the version and a hash of every file, which marks the directory as installed by this package.\n3. Runs `hermes plugins validate` on the directory. If `hermes` rejects it, `install` exits with `hermes`'s exit code. If `hermes` isn't on `PATH`, it exits 1 with a clear error.\n\nThe code is in `src/` (`cli.ts`, `install.ts`, `manifest.ts`, `hermes.ts`, `package.ts`) and compiles to `dist/`, which is gitignored.\n\n**Tests:** `test/harness.ts` gives each test a temporary `HOME` / `HERMES_HOME` and a fake `hermes` first on `PATH`. The fake records the arguments of every call and can be told to fail. `test/install.test.ts` covers the five checklist items. `npm test` now builds, runs the Node tests, then runs the Python test from ticket 02.\n\n**Decisions you might want to revisit:**\n- **Build on publish only:** I used `prepack` to build `dist/`, not `prepare` or `postinstall`, because the spec rules out install hooks.\n- **Version:** `package.json` had no name or version, so I set `hermes-tiiny-router` / `0.0.0`. I set the license to MIT to match the `LICENSE` file.\n- **New dev dependencies:** I added `typescript` (7.x) and `@types/node`.\n- **Node version for development:** the tests are `.ts` files that Node runs directly, which needs Node 22.18 or later. The shipped command still targets Node 20. I noted this in `AGENTS.md`.\n\n**Tests that passed on the first run:** three of the five tests (custom `HERMES_HOME`, installing twice, config and secrets untouched) passed as soon as I wrote them, because the item 1 code already did the right thing. For the `HERMES_HOME` test, I temporarily broke the code to confirm it can fail. The config/secrets test can't fail yet, since `install` doesn't touch either file; it's there to catch a regression once the config step is added.\n\n**Limits of this first version:**\n- Re-installing overwrites files in place and doesn't remove files that a newer version dropped.\n- There's no local-edit check and no `--force` yet; both are later tickets.\n- If validation fails, the copied directory is left in place.\n- The test assumes the secrets file is `$HERMES_HOME/.env`, taken from the install steps in `AGENTS.md`."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":255,"cache_read_input_tokens":67238,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":255},"output_tokens":5,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"68f65b3d-37bb-43c3-9af4-1be0edc7b1a4","uuid":"541c1a7c-a456-4f58-a932-455d6f41f5c6","timestamp":"2026-11-21T05:46:22.644Z","request_id":"req_011ChFYY9RquVa4LwWzBQbhY"}
